@0    = ~"The rotting orb was levitating in the center of a damp cave. A zombie beholder, who was believed to be dead for a century, or mayhap more. Undead and wild, at the very same time. When it saw any living creature, it would bite them with its powerful maw. This is a dead magic area, so it was used to fighting the unfortunate with its sharp teeth."~
@1    = ~A zombie beholder? And most likely an angered one. It deserves to be destroyed, and that is exactly what we should do to it.~
@2    = ~This one can only be faced in a one-on-one battle. That is why the fee for this one isn't 3,500 gold pieces, but slightly lower: 3,000 coins, and you may face it. The same person will learn from that book.~
@3    = ~Fine. It's only fair for the original leader, <PLAYER1>, to face this thing.~
@4    = ~Fine. <PLAYER2> shall face this thing.~
@5    = ~Fine. <PLAYER3> shall face this thing.~
@6    = ~Fine. <PLAYER4> shall face this thing.~
@7    = ~Fine. <PLAYER5> shall face this thing.~
@8    = ~Fine. <PLAYER6> shall face this thing.~
@9    = ~No. I'll pass. At least for now.~
@10   = ~Of course! So, let's start the process.~
@11   = ~"After years of haunting the cave system, the grotesque zombie beholder is finally dead, and no creatures shall become victims of its insatiable appetite."~
@12   = ~The one who fought this monster shall be the one to receive the gift.~
@13   = ~You've already faced the battle this book describes.~